% A 2-of-3 multisig (P2WSH)
%
% The Logical English twin of a Bitcoin spending policy, written by the
% Miniscript translator. Who can spend the
% coin, when, and why: each rule is one spending path of the policy.
%
% Source: the Bitcoin Core descriptor documentation
%         https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/doc/descriptors.md
%
% The source, as written (cut into lines of 100 characters: join them for the text):
%     wsh(multi(2,03a0434d9e47f3c86235477c7b1ae6ae5d3442d49b1943c2b752a68e2a47e247c7,03774ae7f858a9411e5ef
%     4246b70c65aac5649980be5c17891bbec17895da008cb,03d01115d548e7561b15c38f004d734633687cf4419620095bc5b0
%     f47070afe85a))
%
% The source, laid out (keys and hashes by their role, <like this>):
%     wsh(multi(2,<cosigner A>,<cosigner B>,<cosigner C>))
%
% The legend (role <- key or hash as written in the source):
%     cosigner A <- 03a0434d9e47f3c86235477c7b1ae6ae5d3442d49b1943c2b752a68e2a47e247c7
%     cosigner B <- 03774ae7f858a9411e5ef4246b70c65aac5649980be5c17891bbec17895da008cb
%     cosigner C <- 03d01115d548e7561b15c38f004d734633687cf4419620095bc5b0f47070afe85a
%
% What it says (the spending policy, by BIP 379's semantics):
%     at least 2 of these 3:
%       a signature by cosigner A
%       a signature by cosigner B
%       a signature by cosigner C
%
% Try it in Minsc (the policy compiled to Miniscript, Script and an address,
% in the browser): the document "the policy in Minsc" below.
%
