    spendable expects answers [].

scenario flip_now is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, no delay passed
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner A", "add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner B"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner B", "add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner C"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner A", "add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner C"]].

scenario flip_after_delays is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, every delay passed
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner A", "add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner B"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner B", "add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner C"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner A", "add: the witness contains a signature by cosigner C"]].

scenario lost_cosigner_A is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of cosigner A lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by cosigner B.
    the witness contains a signature by cosigner C.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the witness contains a signature by cosigner B"], ["remove: the witness contains a signature by cosigner C"]].

scenario lost_cosigner_B is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of cosigner B lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by cosigner A.
    the witness contains a signature by cosigner C.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the witness contains a signature by cosigner A"], ["remove: the witness contains a signature by cosigner C"]].

scenario lost_cosigner_C is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of cosigner C lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by cosigner A.
    the witness contains a signature by cosigner B.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the witness contains a signature by cosigner A"], ["remove: the witness contains a signature by cosigner B"]].

